{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_fdfblodi5bb2kkszbkbm23gn3t3q26ai5egouogklmaiz5cfajiq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — all four phases pass.\n\n## Results\n\n**Phase A artifacts** (`translation/`): `SYMBOLS.md` (38 symbols), `ERRORS.md` (40 rejection rows), `CONFIGS.md` (72 configuration rows), plus `MUTATION.md`.\n\n**Phase D symbol parity:** `nm -D` diff between the C `.so` and Rust `.so` is **empty in both directions** — 38/38 exported, 0 unresolved non-libc imports. No module was missing; `c_src/src/lib.c` is a single TU and every external-linkage function has a real Rust body.\n\n**Tests** (`translation/tests/`, 107 tests, all loading *both* `.so`s via `libloading`):\n- `valid_paths.rs` — 68 tests, one per CONFIGS row 1–69, ~4000 randomized inputs/row (fixed seed)\n- `stress.rs` — 3 tests, rows 70–72: 250k-sample `c2GJK`/`c2Collided` cross-products + 200k composed `c22→c23→c2D/c2L/c2Witness` pipelines\n- `error_paths.rs` — 32 tests covering all 40 ERRORS rows, incl. out-of-range `C2_TYPE` values across FFI, NULL pointers, negative/oversized counts, `div == 0`, NaN/inf/±0/subnormals\n- `symbols.rs` — 4 tests: `nm` diff, unresolved-symbol allowlist, proof the harness loads two *distinct* libraries, and a negative control proving `same()` can fail\n\n**Zero divergences found.** All 107 tests pass against the default (`-O0`) *and* `-O2` C builds, under both feature configurations (`Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`; `run_all.sh` enumerates the power set and runs default + `--no-default-features`). No binary target exists, so the stdout gate is N/A.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n1. **Test-suite sensitivity was verified, not assumed.** `mutation_check.sh` injects 28 deliberate bugs into `src/lib.rs`: **25 killed**. The 3 survivors are *proved equivalent* in `MUTATION.md` — e.g. the `while (iter < 20)` cap is unreachable (a 4M-sample probe found max 5 iterations, since both proxies hold ≤4 verts), so `stress.rs` asserts the C/Rust iteration histograms match *and* that nothing above 5 appears, which will fire if that ever changes.\n\n2. **One genuine C-side landmine, documented not \"fixed\".** A caller-supplied `c2GJKCache` whose `iA[i] >= pA.count` (e.g. index 1 with a CIRCLE proxy) makes C read its **uninitialised stack** `c2Proxy`, which Rust zeroes. This is the only construction that makes the two disagree, and it is unspecifiable rather than a translation bug — the Rust was left alone and `ERRORS.md` records it in the excluded-UB table.\n\nI also added a staleness guard: the harness refuses to run if either `.so` is older than its source, so a rebuilt-but-not-retested artifact can't silently vacuously pass (it caught exactly that during this session)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5348,"cache_read_input_tokens":164925,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5348,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"269dae8c-83b7-4194-b947-025790418744","uuid":"8b3e752e-4271-4987-995e-e3c64d758936","timestamp":"2026-09-05T11:10:38.245Z"}
